# Sorcerous Spyglass: as it enters Bot1 looks at Bot2's hand (CR 614.12a) and names Wasteland (any card name, CR 201.4). From
# then on no Wasteland's destroy ability can be activated, by Bot1 (the Spyglass's own controller) or by Bot2 (CR 602.5), but
# the {T}: Add {C} ability of each can (a mana ability, CR 605.1a). Strip Mine, not the chosen name, still destroys Bot1's
# Wasteland on turn 4: the positive control that Bot2's activated abilities in general are untouched.

[Bot1 Deck]
Wasteland
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Sorcerous Spyglass
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Wasteland
Strip Mine
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Wasteland.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Wasteland.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sorcerous Spyglass.Cast
Bot1.Name(Wasteland)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Sorcerous Spyglass.ChosenName = Wasteland
! Bot1.Battlefield.Wasteland.Activate(Ability: Destroy)
Bot1.Battlefield.Wasteland.Activate(Ability: #1)
? Bot1.Mana = {C}
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
! Bot2.Battlefield.Wasteland.Activate(Ability: Destroy)
Bot2.Battlefield.Wasteland.Activate(Ability: #1)
? Bot2.Mana = {C}
Bot2.Hand.Strip Mine.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Strip Mine.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Wasteland; Ability: Destroy)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Turn = 4
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Mox Pearl; Sorcerous Spyglass
Bot1.Graveyard = Wasteland
Bot2.Battlefield = Wasteland
Bot2.Graveyard = Strip Mine
